.TH LLAPI_FID2PATH_AT 3 2026-10-26 "Lustre User API" "Lustre Library Functions"
.SH NAME
llapi_fid2path_at \- resolve a File Identifier to a pathname
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
.PP
.BI "int llapi_fid2path_at(int " mnt_fd ", const struct lu_fid *" fid ", char *" path ","
.BI "                      int " pathlen ", long long *" recno ", int *" linkno ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR llapi_fid2path_at()
stores the pathname corresponding to the given File Identifier
.I fid
into
.IR path .
.I pathlen
is the size of
.I path
in bytes, including the NUL terminator.
The lookup is performed relative to the filesystem referenced by
.IR mnt_fd .
If
.I linkno
is non-NULL, it is used to select and return a specific hardlink of the FID.
Links are counted starting at 0.
On success, if another hardlink exists after the returned hardlink,
the value pointed to by
.I linkno
is incremented.
If no more hardlinks exist,
.RI * linkno
is left unchanged.
If
.I linkno
is NULL, the first link is returned.
If
.RI * linkno
is greater than or equal to the number of hardlinks,
the first link is returned and
.RI * linkno
is left unchanged.
The
.I recno
parameter is currently ignored,
and if it is non-NULL the value it points to is left unchanged.
.SH RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
.B -EBADF
.I mnt_fd
is an invalid file descriptor.
.TP
.B -EINVAL
An invalid FID was passed in
.IR fid .
.TP
.B -ENOENT
The FID does not exist.
.TP
.B -ENOMEM
Not enough memory to process the request.
.TP
.B -ENOTTY
.I mnt_fd
refers to an object that does not support this operation.
.TP
.B -EOVERFLOW
.I path
is not big enough for pathname resolution.
.TP
.B -EPERM
The caller lacks
.B CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH
capability, and the
.B user_fid2path
mount option is not enabled.
.TP
.B -ERANGE
.I path
is not big enough to hold the returned path.
.SH EXAMPLES
This prints all of the hardlinks of a file.
Paths are printed relative to the filesystem root.
The
.I mount_fd
argument comes from
.BR llapi_root_path_open (3):
.PP
.EX
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
\&
void print_paths(int mount_fd, struct lu_fid fid)
{
	int linkno = 0;
	int linktmp;
	int rc;
\&
	do {
		char path[4096] = { 0 };
\&
		linktmp = linkno;
\&
		rc = llapi_fid2path_at(mount_fd, &fid, path, sizeof(path),
		                       NULL, &linkno);
		if (rc) {
			fprintf(stderr, "llapi_fid2path_at(): %s\\n", strerror(-rc));
			return;
		}
\&
		printf("%s\\n", path);
	} while (linktmp != linkno);
}
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llapi_fid2path_at()
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
user application interface library since release 2.14.50
.\" Added in commit v2_14_50-43-gc45558bf56
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llapi_fid2path (3),
.BR llapi_root_path_open (3),
.BR llapi_layout (7),
.BR lustreapi (7)
